0..60 Comment "/// This source winds a loop word at three lengths of cctt\'s"
61..137 Comment "/// `tests/bench/s1.cctt`. There the winding transports zero along a word of"
138..195 Comment "/// loops in the helix, and `forceℤ` forces the result."
196..199 Comment "///"
200..278 Comment "/// gandr presents the loop space of the circle by its words. The winding of a"
279..356 Comment "/// word is `wind`, which counts its letters. Each run writes the word, winds"
357..395 Comment "/// it and forces the integer to `Tt`."
396..399 Comment "///"
400..478 Comment "/// The run machine runs each length that this source states. At 10⁶ letters"
479..557 Comment "/// the run spends its jump budget before it settles. With a larger budget, it"
558..630 Comment "/// settles within `--memory 1GiB`. The machine does not run a word that"
631..698 Comment "/// `Path.step` composes, because it does not lower that transport."
699..702 Comment "///"
703..719 Comment "/// - see: #6309"
720..791 Comment "/// - see: #6324 — the memory bound of the heap and the window region"
792..845 Comment "/// - see: #6325 — the jump budget at 10⁶ letters"
